WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.002
-Our next guests are
Emmy-nominated writers

00:00:03.002 --> 00:00:04.804
whose work you know from
"Saturday Night Live."

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:06.005
Their new show, "The Other Two,"

00:00:06.005 --> 00:00:08.174
premieres Thursday night
on Comedy Central.

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:09.609
Let's take a look.

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:13.079
-Hey, guys, it's your captains
speaking -- Tiff and Amanda.

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:14.713
Sorry about the turbulence,

00:00:14.713 --> 00:00:17.750
but from now on we're expecting
such a smooth ride.

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:19.519
So relax and enjoy the flight.

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:20.953
-Bye!

00:00:20.953 --> 00:00:22.488
-Oh, no.

00:00:22.488 --> 00:00:26.025
Our pilot's name is Tiff?

00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:28.160
-Oh, what, a woman
can't be a pilot?

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.729
-Okay.
-Wow, gay misogyny is real.

00:00:30.729 --> 00:00:33.500
-No, a woman can be my pilot,
all right?

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:36.736
Meryl Streep can be my pilot.
Viola Davis can be my pilot.

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:39.105
-You'd rather have Viola Davis,
the actress,

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:41.273
than two actual pilots?

00:00:41.273 --> 00:00:43.376
-Hey, guys, sorry to bug,

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:46.379
but we have now reached
cruising altitude.

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:49.349
-So, feel free to unbuckle
and move about the cabin.

00:00:49.349 --> 00:00:50.883
-Bye!

00:00:50.883 --> 00:00:53.353
-I know you know what I mean.
-No. No, I don't. I don't.

00:00:53.353 --> 00:00:55.755
-They said bye at the same time.

00:00:55.755 --> 00:00:57.624
-Please welcome to the show
my friends

00:00:57.624 --> 00:00:59.492
Chris Kelly and
Sarah Schneider, everyone!

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:01.060
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:11.070
♪♪

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:16.142
♪♪

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:17.777
Welcome, you two!
-Wow!

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:20.480
-Oh, my God!
-I'm so happy to have you here.

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:22.681
We have been friends
for a long time,

00:01:22.681 --> 00:01:25.051
because we all wrote together
at "Saturday Night Live."

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:26.018
-Yeah.
-We did.

00:01:26.018 --> 00:01:27.553
-And you were head writers
together

00:01:27.553 --> 00:01:29.655
during the election year
of 2016.

00:01:29.655 --> 00:01:30.923
-We absolutely were.

00:01:30.923 --> 00:01:33.292
-Now, I was a head writer
during 2008,

00:01:33.292 --> 00:01:36.328
which was similar in that
it was a bit of a circus.

00:01:36.328 --> 00:01:39.265
The difference was, on election
night, the circus ended.

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:41.734
-Yeah.
-In 2008.

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.769
But not for you guys.
-No.

00:01:43.769 --> 00:01:46.072
-You had to keep writing
all those sketches.

00:01:46.072 --> 00:01:48.507
-I know. We would keep trying
to write, like --

00:01:48.507 --> 00:01:50.776
we love writing nostalgic
sketches about, like,

00:01:50.776 --> 00:01:53.245
going home
and high school theater.

00:01:53.245 --> 00:01:55.581
And we would keep trying
to write those sketches.

00:01:55.581 --> 00:01:58.984
And every single week, we would
be on the set loving it,

00:01:58.984 --> 00:02:00.753
and, like, our phones
would buzz.

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:02.755
-We'd be like, "It's him again."

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:03.923
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:06.492
"He has ruined our week for us."
-The fun is over.

00:02:06.492 --> 00:02:08.595
-Well, so, you did a sketch
that I love

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:10.563
called "Crucible Cast Party."
-Yeah.

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:13.199
-This might actually be
you checking your phone.

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:14.433
-This is mid-moment.

00:02:14.433 --> 00:02:16.803
-Okay. So, what were you seeing
on your phone?

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:19.538
-So, we were making
a fun musical with all the girls

00:02:19.538 --> 00:02:22.008
about a high school party.

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:24.077
And then we got the alert --

00:02:24.077 --> 00:02:26.713
the "Access Hollywood" tape
had come out.

00:02:26.713 --> 00:02:27.946
-Yeah.

00:02:27.946 --> 00:02:30.449
-And so, we were both just like,
"Oh, God damn it!"

00:02:30.449 --> 00:02:32.352
So, that's a photo of one woman

00:02:32.352 --> 00:02:34.720
having a blast
making a music video.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:37.457
And then another man
in the deepest of hells

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:40.926
trying to write a cold open
in 45 minutes on Friday night

00:02:40.926 --> 00:02:43.228
at 3:00 in the morning.
-Yes, because things were

00:02:43.228 --> 00:02:46.065
happening that you had to throw
away what you had for Saturday

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:48.400
on Friday, which rarely
happened in my time there.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:49.569
This was also great.

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:51.437
You guys wrote
the Bernie Sanders sketches

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:55.008
where Larry David played Bernie
Sanders, which is fantastic.

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:56.141
[ Applause ]

00:02:56.141 --> 00:03:00.713
Such a wonderful person,
but before you meet him,

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:02.614
you think he might be, like,
really irascible

00:03:02.614 --> 00:03:04.384
and maybe not fun to work with.

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:05.918
But he was great, right?
-He was lovely.

00:03:05.918 --> 00:03:07.920
We did this
"Bern your enthusiasm" parody,

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:11.624
and on Saturday night,
right before dress, we heard,

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:14.093
"Oh, Larry wants to come up
and watch a cut of the video."

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:16.762
And we were like, "Oh, no,
I don't want that to happen.

00:03:16.762 --> 00:03:17.997
I don't want to watch us

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:20.065
do a parody of his own show
next to him."

00:03:20.065 --> 00:03:21.367
It was very nerve-racking,

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:23.336
but he laughed
through the whole thing

00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:24.770
and was so positive and nice.

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:27.406
And I was like, "This isn't how
you're supposed to be.

00:03:27.406 --> 00:03:28.874
You're supposed to hate this."

00:03:28.874 --> 00:03:31.610
-Well, he did send us an e-mail
afterwards that was titled,

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:33.713
"Thanks," and basically
the gist of it was,

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:36.549
"I had a great time except for
all of the packing and flying.

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:38.951
And I like you guys
but I don't really want to see

00:03:38.951 --> 00:03:39.986
you guys again soon."

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:41.687
-And we were like,
"There he is."

00:03:41.687 --> 00:03:43.590
-That's what we signed up for.
-That's what we wanted.

